On Fri, Sep 17, 2010 at 1:31 PM, Stela Selckiku <selckiku@gmail.com> wrote:

> What are the various things that are "jukni"?  Do we not even agree on
> that?

Among the arachnids, we have mites, ticks, scorpions and things that
look like them, and harvestmen (daddy-long-legs) in addition to
spiders proper.

Among the non-insect arthropods, we have the crustaceans, the
horseshoe crabs, the sea spiders, and the myriapods (centipedes and
millipedes).  Trilobites are extinct but somewhat well known to the
public.

These lists are not exhaustive.  Google Images should help in finding
pictures, or Wikimedia Commons if you want free ones.



